  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116226",
      "title": "Converting Observables To Signals",
      "lectureOrder": 215,
      "videoOrder": 206,
      "sourceHash": "e817a9e60fb4fe3a68eaba432f6145046e7cd12de67c4f531d46cc0ca5851232",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.48,
          "end": 3.51,
          "en": "Now just as you can convert signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.51,
          "end": 8.04,
          "en": "to observables or listen to signals with observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.04,
          "end": 12.03,
          "en": "you can of course also go into the other direction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.03,
          "end": 13.62,
          "en": "and we could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.62,
          "end": 17.04,
          "en": "re-add our interval observable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.04,
          "end": 19.863,
          "en": "but now as a property for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.91,
          "end": 23.58,
          "en": "And therefore I'll also add the dollar sign here at the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.58,
          "end": 27.87,
          "en": "of this name and create that observable by calling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.87,
          "end": 31.44,
          "en": "that interval function that is provided by RxJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.44,
          "end": 34.383,
          "en": "And I'll set it to 1000 milliseconds again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.06,
          "end": 37.71,
          "en": "Now just like that, nothing will happen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.71,
          "end": 39.9,
          "en": "because as I mentioned, you need to subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.9,
          "end": 41.583,
          "en": "for something to happen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.72,
          "end": 45.48,
          "en": "But here I actually don't want to subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.48,
          "end": 49.8,
          "en": "Instead, I now wanna convert this observable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.8,
          "end": 51.42,
          "en": "to a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.42,
          "end": 55.77,
          "en": "or I wanna create a new Signal to be precise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.77,
          "end": 57.6,
          "en": "that in the end gets updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.6,
          "end": 61.593,
          "en": "whenever this observable here produces a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.24,
          "end": 65.58,
          "en": "For that I'll add the interval Signal then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.58,
          "end": 67.5,
          "en": "as an additional property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.5,
          "end": 72.42,
          "en": "because just as with two observable, you have to convert",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.42,
          "end": 74.67,
          "en": "that observable to a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.67,
          "end": 77.91,
          "en": "or set up that listener in a place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.91,
          "end": 80.88,
          "en": "where you could also inject a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.88,
          "end": 83.46000000000001,
          "en": "So either here when setting up a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.46000000000001,
          "end": 84.93,
          "en": "or in the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.93,
          "end": 88.263,
          "en": "and here, I'll do it here when setting up the properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 90.18,
          "end": 93.843,
          "en": "And I'll then use the two Signal function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.68,
          "end": 99.68,
          "en": "which is also imported from Angular core RxJS interop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.62,
          "end": 104.88,
          "en": "and pass my RxJS observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.88,
          "end": 108.45,
          "en": "this interval dollar sign to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.45,
          "end": 112.023,
          "en": "And that will now give me a Signal based on this observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.94,
          "end": 115.14,
          "en": "And of course with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 115.14,
          "end": 117.72,
          "en": "we can now use it like any other Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 117.72,
          "end": 122.55,
          "en": "with the effect function with the computed function and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 122.55,
          "end": 125.61,
          "en": "or by outputting it in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.61,
          "end": 127.06,
          "en": "And that's what I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.92,
          "end": 131.76,
          "en": "I'll output my interval Signal like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.76,
          "end": 134.433,
          "en": "like any other Signal in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.5,
          "end": 138.21,
          "en": "And if you do that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 138.21,
          "end": 140.57999999999998,
          "en": "you'll notice one interesting thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 140.57999999999998,
          "end": 144.51,
          "en": "If you watch here where that number is output, if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 144.51,
          "end": 147.12,
          "en": "you see initially there's nothing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.12,
          "end": 151.86,
          "en": "It takes a short while until we see that zero appear.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 151.86,
          "end": 153.21,
          "en": "And the reason for that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.21,
          "end": 156.32999999999998,
          "en": "and one important difference between observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.32999999999998,
          "end": 159.6,
          "en": "and signals is that observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.6,
          "end": 163.473,
          "en": "unlike signals have no initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 164.43,
          "end": 166.56,
          "en": "Now subjects can be different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.56,
          "end": 169.95,
          "en": "You can create subjects that have an initial value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.95,
          "end": 172.71,
          "en": "but observables like the observable created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 172.71,
          "end": 174.84,
          "en": "by calling the interval function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.84,
          "end": 177.69299999999998,
          "en": "those have no initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.77,
          "end": 183.36,
          "en": "Signals on the other hand, always have some initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 183.36,
          "end": 187.26,
          "en": "Sure, you could set that initial value to undefined or null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 187.26,
          "end": 189.99,
          "en": "but they do have some initial value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.99,
          "end": 192.39,
          "en": "Observables do not have that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 192.39,
          "end": 194.43,
          "en": "and therefore as a workaround,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 194.43,
          "end": 198.32999999999998,
          "en": "Angular will set the special undefined value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.32999999999998,
          "end": 202.713,
          "en": "as an initial value for a Signal created with two Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 204.03,
          "end": 207.24,
          "en": "Now you might want a different initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 207.24,
          "end": 209.64,
          "en": "and that's why when using two Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.64,
          "end": 212.79,
          "en": "you can pass a second argument to that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 212.79,
          "end": 215.28300000000002,
          "en": "and pass in a configuration object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.39,
          "end": 220.14,
          "en": "There you can configure various things like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 220.14,
          "end": 223.02,
          "en": "manual cleanup to which I'll get back in a second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.02,
          "end": 225.66,
          "en": "but you can also set an initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 225.66,
          "end": 230.223,
          "en": "and set this to zero, for example, to override that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 231.57,
          "end": 234.66,
          "en": "By doing that, you would now see that even if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 234.66,
          "end": 238.02,
          "en": "we see the number zero right from the start instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 238.02,
          "end": 239.7,
          "en": "of seeing nothing initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 239.7,
          "end": 243.06,
          "en": "And that's just also something you should keep in mind.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 243.06,
          "end": 247.98,
          "en": "Observables do not necessarily have an initial value Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 247.98,
          "end": 249.453,
          "en": "on the other hand do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 250.5,
          "end": 254.43,
          "en": "Now two Signal does one other nice thing for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 254.43,
          "end": 259.43,
          "en": "It will automatically clean up the observable subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 259.59,
          "end": 262.83,
          "en": "if the component where you are using that Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 262.83,
          "end": 266.553,
          "en": "that was created with two Signal gets removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 267.42,
          "end": 271.38,
          "en": "So when using two Signal on an observable in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 271.38,
          "end": 275.15999999999997,
          "en": "you don't need to clean up that subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 275.15999999999997,
          "end": 276.603,
          "en": "or that observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 277.44,
          "end": 280.38,
          "en": "You could disable this built-in behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 280.38,
          "end": 282.87,
          "en": "by setting manual cleanup to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 282.87,
          "end": 285.594,
          "en": "In that case, you would have to make sure that you dispose",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 285.594,
          "end": 290.13,
          "en": "of that observable manually if the component gets removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.13,
          "end": 291.693,
          "en": "But you don't have to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
